    aiContent: {
      difficulty: {
        easy: 'Plays to win every trick as in a normal trick-taking game; wastes Aces and 10s early; often loses the final trick due to card depletion.',
        medium: 'Understands that only the final trick matters. Attempts to preserve one strong card for the end but makes occasional tactical errors in suit depletion.',
        hard: 'Tracks all played cards and remaining hands. Calculates which opponents still hold cards in each suit. Optimally forces opponents to exhaust high cards early, then leads the final trick with a card guaranteed to win (or with a 3 in Cameroon variant to maximize stakes). Models opponent hand compositions from lead patterns.',
      },
      considerations: [
        "AI must prioritize 'Final Trick Victory' over cumulative trick count, inverting normal trick-taking logic.",
        'AI must evaluate the cost of winning early tricks in terms of lead control for the final trick.',
        'In Cameroon variant, AI must weight the value of winning with a 3 (higher multiplier) versus playing a guaranteed-win high card.',
      ],
